<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_Miasma_StrangeTier.xml           UtinniPatches - MIASMA_MECHANICS_1 M5 build pass

  miasma_kit_spec.md M5's own table, 1% tier - "the genuinely strange tier."
  The spec's own section text (M5 body paragraph) still calls this tier
  "content deliberately unspecified here - owner card 1," but that line is
  STALE: the spec's own "Owner cards - RULED, sitting 2026-09-12" section,
  just below it in the same file, shows card 1 was fully ruled in a bench
  sitting the next day - five named strange-tier HediffDefs with full
  mechanical descriptions, Tide-reader explicitly CUT. Same stale-header
  shape FORGE_MECHANICS_1 hit once already; the RULED section is the one
  followed here, per this item's own build assignment. All five: HediffDefs
  only (ban #1 - never genes, never a directed pick), none healing, all
  framed as wild-nature biology, never Force-register.

  Each hediff below notes, inline, exactly which half of its ruled
  description is real mechanism this pass and which half is an honest gap -
  see MIASMA_MECHANICS_1.md's own "M5 build pass" section for the full
  accounting across all five.
-->
<Defs>

  <!--
    Swarm-marked - ruled text: "the karr-clade fever-swarms stop reading the
    pawn as prey: swarms don't attack them, swarm-contact disease exposure
    drops to a trickle. Fiction stays biological (scent-kin, not blessing)."

    BOTH behavioral halves need a fever-swarm mechanism to hook into and
    NONE exists yet anywhere in src/RimMandrake or src/RimUtinni (checked
    this pass: grep -rn "swarm" -i turned up only unrelated content -
    ShipVermin, CreatureBehaviors' vermin pressure, PawnFlavor backstories -
    nothing that is or drives a Miasma fever-swarm). The spec's own M2
    ("the breath-tide surge") is the only mechanic in this kit that could
    ever own a swarm entity, and M2 is not built - owed there, not invented
    here as a new AI system (out of this pass's scope, per its own
    instruction). RM_HediffComp_EnvironmentalExposure (M4, already shipped)
    has no per-pawn stat hook at all - its severity math reads only weather
    + M1 salinity band, never GetStatValue - so there is no existing lever
    "swarm-contact exposure drops to a trickle" could even patch into today.

    What ships instead: a small, real, buildable stand-in for "the pilgrims'
    biology resists common exposure ailments a little" - the same
    ImmunityGainSpeed lever the 30% tier uses (RUT_Miasma_HardenedImmunity.xml),
    at a level between that tier's 0.20 and the 14% tier's smaller offsets,
    since this is the rare 1% roll. This is flavor-adjacent, not the ruled
    swarm behavior - flagged, not silently substituted.
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RUT_Miasma_SwarmMarked</defName>
    <label>swarm-marked</label>
    <description>Something about you reads as kin to the karr-clade swarms now - scent, warmth, the Working under your skin. It shows in small ways. The bigger claim (that the swarms themselves let you pass) waits on the swarms existing at all.</description>
    <hediffClass>Hediff</hediffClass>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <statOffsets>
          <ImmunityGainSpeed>0.10</ImmunityGainSpeed>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

  <!--
    Salt-blooded - ruled text: "bleed rate halved, food-poisoning
    near-immune, corpse barely rots; pain sensitivity up a notch.
    Preservation, not healing."

    Bleed and pain confirmed real, clean vanilla HediffStage fields (checked
    this pass against Verse/HediffStage.cs and Verse/HediffSet.cs's
    CalculateBleedRate/CalculatePain):
      totalBleedFactor  multiplies HediffSet.BleedRateTotal directly
                        (HediffSet.cs:1299-1324) - "bleed rate halved" is
                        exactly totalBleedFactor 0.5, no invented mechanism.
      painFactor        multiplies the pawn's total computed pain
                        (HediffSet.CalculatePain) - "pain sensitivity up a
                        notch" is painFactor > 1.

    Food-poisoning resistance and corpse rot checked and NOT built - no
    stat-level lever exists for either in the live 1.6 decompile:
      - Food poisoning has no per-eater resistance stat at all. The only
        real hook (RimWorld/FoodUtility.cs:1374,
        TryGetFoodPoisoningChanceOverrideFromTraits) is keyed per specific
        food ThingDef via Trait.CurrentData.ingestibleModifiers, not a
        general hediff-level lever; FoodPoisoning itself
        (Data/Core/Defs/HediffDefs/Hediffs_Global_Misc.xml) has no
        HediffCompProperties_Immunizable, so ImmunityGainSpeed does not
        touch it either.
      - Corpse rot rate (RimWorld/CompRottable.cs) is driven purely by
        GenTemperature.RotRateAtTemperature - no GetStatValue call
        anywhere in that class, and TicksToRotStart is a flat per-ThingDef
        value baked once per race, not something a living pawn's hediff can
        reach.
    Both would need a Harmony patch (on CompFoodPoisonable/FoodUtility and
    on CompRottable respectively) - out of this pass's "clean XML hediff"
    scope; not guessed at with a fabricated stat name, flagged instead.
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RUT_Miasma_SaltBlooded</defName>
    <label>salt-blooded</label>
    <description>The brine got further into you than it should have. Your blood barely wants to leave your body, and pain doesn't slow you the way it used to. Preservation, not healing - something in you keeps a little longer than it should.</description>
    <hediffClass>Hediff</hediffClass>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <totalBleedFactor>0.5</totalBleedFactor>
        <painFactor>1.15</painFactor>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

  <!--
    Loam-lunged - ruled text: "the pawn exhales a trace of the Working:
    slightly faster plant growth immediately around their sleeping/working
    spots, delta-loam fertility developing where they rest. PASSIVE AND
    TINY - the line against the Greentide/explosive-growth soak territory
    is that this never triggers, never surges, never scales."

    Genuinely novel behavior, no vanilla stat or existing RM_ comp does
    this (checked this pass - see RM_HediffComp_LocalGrowthAura.cs's own
    header for what was checked and ruled out). New, small, generic C#:
    RM_HediffComp_LocalGrowthAura, a direct crib of
    HediffComp_PeriodicAreaAttack's radius-scan shape substituting a
    Plant.Growth nudge for damage. Values below match that comp's own
    documented defaults, written out explicit for citation.
  -->
  <HediffDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_Miasma_LoamLunged</defName>
    <label>loam-lunged</label>
    <description>Every breath carries a trace of the Working out of you. Nothing anyone would notice looking - but wherever you rest a while, the ground remembers it, just a little.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.CompProperties_LocalGrowthAura">
        <radius>3</radius>
        <tickIntervalTicks>2500</tickIntervalTicks>
        <growthPerCycle>0.002</growthPerCycle>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </HediffDef>

  <!--
    Mother-dreamed - ruled text: "rarely, a day-long harmless fever-dream
    ending in a random vanilla Inspiration. Letter text is wild-nature,
    never oracle/mystic register."

    Checked this pass before writing any new C# (per the spec's own
    "check for a stock HediffComp before writing new C#"): no stock
    HediffComp grants a random Inspiration on an MTB, but the exact real
    seam vanilla content already uses for "give this pawn a random
    Inspiration" is documented in full in
    RM_HediffComp_PeriodicInspiration.cs's own header
    (InspirationHandler.TryStartInspiration +
    GetRandomAvailableInspirationDef, cribbed from
    IngestionOutcomeDoer_Psilocap.cs and CompAbilityEffect_GiveInspiration.cs).
    New comp is a thin MTB-roll wrapper around that real API, nothing
    invented about the inspiration grant itself.

    letterLabelKey/letterTextKey point at translation keys not yet added to
    a Languages/ folder - same owed gap this item's own M4 pass already
    flagged for RM_MiasmaBoonLetterLabel/Text; .Translate() falls back to
    the raw key rather than erroring, so this does not block anything.
  -->
  <HediffDef MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_Miasma_MotherDreamed</defName>
    <label>mother-dreamed</label>
    <description>Once in a great while, the fever brings a dream - long, strange, and harmless. You wake with your hands already knowing what to do next. Wild-nature, not oracle: nothing in the haze speaks to you, it just leaves the door open sometimes.</description>
    <hediffClass>HediffWithComps</hediffClass>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <comps>
      <li Class="RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.CompProperties_PeriodicInspiration">
        <mtbDaysToDream>20</mtbDaysToDream>
        <letterLabelKey>RUT_MotherDreamedLetterLabel</letterLabelKey>
        <letterTextKey>RUT_MotherDreamedLetterText</letterTextKey>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </HediffDef>

  <!--
    Fever-tempered - ruled text: "the fever recalibrated the thermostat:
    the pawn's comfortable temperature band permanently widens both
    directions (magnitude tuned at build). Replacement for the cut
    Tide-reader ... pays game-wide on a planet whose geography is
    temperature."

    Plain vanilla HediffStage statOffsets on ComfyTemperatureMin (confirmed
    real, RimWorld/StatDefOf.cs; defaultBaseValue 0, Temperature format) and
    ComfyTemperatureMax (defaultBaseValue 40) - "both directions" is a
    negative offset on Min and a positive offset on Max together. Magnitude
    5C each direction is this pass's own INVENTED tuning value, per the
    ruling's own "tuned at build."
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>RUT_Miasma_FeverTempered</defName>
    <label>fever-tempered</label>
    <description>The fever recalibrated something. Heat and cold both bother you a little less than they used to - not dramatically, but on a world this hot, every degree counts.</description>
    <hediffClass>Hediff</hediffClass>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <tendable>false</tendable>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <statOffsets>
          <ComfyTemperatureMin>-5</ComfyTemperatureMin>
          <ComfyTemperatureMax>5</ComfyTemperatureMax>
        </statOffsets>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>

</Defs>
